NEXT-139	TS-DEVOPS-02 - Split monolith into NextTrade backend, Insights backend, and Identity Service	Done	Platform Foundations	NEXT-8	5	Medium	Kevin	Ilhan Gelle	Sprint 5	Backend, Database, DevOps, Should, cross-cutting, platform	2026-09-07	2026-09-28	Business Requirement: cross-cutting (Should) — no single BR; this is target-state platform architecture, not a feature requirement. Does not block Sprint 4 delivery.  Source: Whiteboard architecture diagram (attach photo to this ticket for reference).  Target Architecture  Two Angular frontends, each its own deployable, each with its own port:  • NextTrade (Angular) — client-facing trading app • NextTrade Insights (Angular) — internal analytics/reporting app  Three backend services, each its own deployable, each with its own port:  • NextTrade backend (Spring Boot) — serves the NextTrade frontend; calls Identity Service for auth • Insights backend (Spring Boot) — serves the NextTrade Insights frontend; calls Identity Service for auth • Identity Service (NestJS) — owns registration, login, JWT issuance/validation, session management; called by both other backends  Shared data layer:  • One Postgres instance, shared by NextTrade backend, Insights backend, and Identity Service  Repo Layout (folded in from the former repo-restructure ticket)  Repo restructured into 5 folders this sprint: NextTrade-backend/, NextTrade-frontend/, NextTradeInsights-backend/, NextTradeInsights-frontend/, auth-service/ (git mv used to preserve history; Insights folders get placeholder READMEs noting Sprint 7). docker-compose.yml, Jenkinsfile, and README.md updated for the new paths.  Why this matters  Today the codebase is a single Spring Boot monolith (see Main.java, UserController, etc. in the lil-leap repo) with all auth code already isolated under com.neueda.leap.user and com.neueda.leap.config. That package boundary is most of the conceptual groundwork for a future Identity Service — this ticket is about actually separating it into its own deployable, plus splitting reporting/analytics into its own backend.  Acceptance Criteria  AC1 Identity Service exists as its own deployable, in auth-service/, exposing registration, login, JWT issuance, and JWT validation.  AC2 NextTrade backend and Insights backend both call Identity Service (not their own local auth logic) to validate incoming requests.  AC3 All three backend services connect to the same shared Postgres instance; each only touches the tables relevant to its domain.  AC4 NextTrade and NextTrade Insights remain separate Angular apps, each pointed at its own backend, each in its own renamed folder (NextTrade-frontend/, NextTradeInsights-frontend/).  AC5 Local dev environment (docker-compose) can spin up all three backends + shared Postgres with one command.  Developer Notes  • This is infrastructure/platform work, not a single-sprint task — expect it to span multiple sprints, though the repo folder rename itself lands in Sprint 5. • Decide early: separate git repos vs. a monorepo with separate build targets. Either works; document the choice here once made. • Service-to-service auth calls (NextTrade backend / Insights backend → Identity Service) need a clear contract (REST + shared JWT verification, or a shared library) — worth a short spike before implementation.  ![](blob:https://media.staging.atl-paas.net/?type=external&localId=b9a2625cdba6&id=&&collection=&height=null&occurrenceKey=null&width=null&__contextId=null&__displayType=null&__external=false&__fileMimeType=null&__fileName=null&__fileSize=null&__mediaTraceId=null&url=blob%3Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fmedia.staging.atl-paas.net%2F%3Ftype%3Dfile%26localId%3Da6bd723788c1%26id%3Dc2d204c4-dc2a-49e0-bbaf-b49fbab8a394%26%26collection%3D%26height%3D884%26occurrenceKey%3Dnull%26width%3D1202%26__contextId%3Dnull%26__displayType%3Dnull%26__external%3Dfalse%26__fileMimeType%3Dnull%26__fileName%3Dnull%26__fileSize%3Dnull%26__mediaTraceId%3Dnull%26url%3Dnull)  ![](blob:https://media.staging.atl-paas.net/?type=exte